'''Mangarla''', also spelt '''Mangala''',  is a [[Pama–Nyungan languages|Pama–Nyungan language]] of [[Western Australia]]. It is spoken by the [[Mangarla people]] of the north-western area of the [[Great Sandy Desert]], inland from the coast.

== Phonology ==
Mangarla's phoneme inventory is typical of Australian languages, and is identical to the inventories of the other Marrngu languages. There are 17 consonant phonemes.<ref name=":0">{{Cite thesis |last=Agnew |first=Brigitte Louise |title=The core of Mangarla grammar |date=2020 |degree=phd |publisher=University of Melbourne |url=https://hdl.handle.net/11343/241927}}</ref>

